## Model card

- **Name:** Exo Free
- **Short description:** An unannounced, anonymous free route on OpenCode Zen that appeared 2026-10-06 (~22:30 UTC) with frontier-flavored specs: ~1M-token context, vision input, reasoning, and tool use at $0. Community fingerprinting points to Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5 underneath (or a router over Claude/GPT), but the true identity is unconfirmed. Effectively deprecated in practice since 2026-10-09 (server returns HTTP 410 while still listed).
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen `opencode/exo-free` via `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/chat/completions` (Chat Completions; `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`). Listed on the live `/zen/v1/models` roster and in the Zen docs pricing table as Free, but a reproduced GitHub issue shows keyless requests fail with `HTTP 410 ModelDeprecated` as of 2026-10-09 (an Oct 8 server routing change, PR #53967, is the suspected cause — see `anomalyco/opencode#54065`).
- **Release / knowledge:** first observed 2026-10-06 22:54 UTC (models.dev sweep); no release date, no knowledge-cutoff statement, no vendor announcement.
- **IDs:** `opencode/exo-free` (the only ID; anonymous — no upstream model card).
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 total / 131,072 max output (models.dev catalog + Zen docs; consistent with `meta.json`).
- **Modalities:** text + image in; text out; reasoning yes (community report: effort fixed at high); tool calling yes; JSON mode yes.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-10):** $0.00 in / out (limited-time free route for feedback collection; Zen privacy notes say free-tier exceptions apply — prompts may be used to improve the model; no zero-data-retention guarantee).
- **Architecture:** unknown/anonymous. No parameter count, no weights. Fingerprint probe (lm.ikale.io, ~300 numeric-generation + tokenizer probes) matched `claude-opus-5.5` at 99.4% confidence (runner-up `claude-fable-5.1` at 0.4%); a closed-set tool, so a distilled Opus imitator or a router ("not a model, but a router with Claude and GPT inside" — community claim) would also match. Leading theories: confidential blind evaluation, routing misconfiguration, or a high-quality distilled model. None confirmed.

