### Negative-findings notes (informal evidence that does NOT qualify as scores)

- Community stress-tests (freeaiapi.org hands-on, 2026-10-07): passed the
  "Pelican on a Bicycle" spatial-reasoning Blender render test and produced a
  working first-shot Blender Python script for a full convenience-store scene
  (aisles, fridges, counters, lighting); accurate diagram-based diagnostics
  for microservice architecture images. Informal pass/fail demos — no harness,
  no percentile, no comparable numbers.
- Fingerprint result (99.4% Opus 5.5 match) measures statistical similarity,
  not capability — explicitly closed-set and spoofable by distillation.
- Volatility: high traffic caused frequent dropouts/429s; endpoint now 410s
  (deprecated server-side) per reproduced issue #54065 — so even the informal
  evidence cannot be re-run.
- Anonymity + no ZDR means any scored row copied from the suspected underlying
  model (Opus 5.5) would be fabrication; scores are therefore not issued.
- When/if the route returns or the identity is confirmed with published
  harness numbers, a new signed file should supersede these notes.

